From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:10:46 -0400
Subject: give tabs an 18 DIP favicon

docs/UI-SPEC.md called for 18 and this project shipped 16, on the grounds that
gfx::kFaviconSize is global and the image would not scale with a bigger slot.
The first half was right and the second was not: TabIcon draws through
DrawImageInt scaled to its bounds, so a bigger slot draws a bigger favicon.

The size is a Stedding parameter used inside tab_icon.cc, so gfx::kFaviconSize
keeps its meaning everywhere else and only tabs change.

Measured by sweeping the parameter against one build: the glyph is 13.5 DIP tall
at 16, 16.5 at 18 and 20.5 at 22, which is the linear response of something
actually being scaled rather than a slot being padded.

Why: it was the last difference from the reference this project had written off
rather than fixed, and the reason given for writing it off was wrong.
Removable when: the tab strip's metrics are themable.
